# A stack closure's block lives in the frame, so refcounting does not govern
# it: xrt_retain and xrt_rc_claim_release_last both no-op on
# XR_OBJ_STORAGE_STACK, so xrt_release returns before reaching the destructor
# that would have released the upvals. Emitting xrt_release here leaked the
# captured cell once per call -- 156 MiB over the 2M-iteration probe.
#
# The captured cell must be released at scope end without freeing the frame
# block, which is what xrt_closure_stack_drop does. Pinning both halves: the
# drop is emitted, and the no-op release is not.
contains=xaot-plan v0
c_contains=xrt_closure_stack_new
c_count=1:xrt_closure_stack_drop(
c_not_regex=xrt_release\(v[0-9]+\); *\n? *return v[0-9]+;
